A promising Barbarian just bit the dust in a most silly way. He had 
finished the Quest, cleared Ludios, had GDSM and reflection and was 
reaping through the dungeon with Vorpal Blade, only to turn to a statue 
at the hissing of a lowly cockatrice. And this after having whacked the 
titan at Medusa's level and all of his buddies with the corpse of 
another cockatrice (which the titan himself helpfully summoned)...

The moral of the story is always to carry a lizard corpse. I didn't have 
a BoH yet, so a lizard corpse was one of the many things I thought I 
could do without, only it turns out that prayer doesn't always help.

